# Both pulse images build from the repository root, so this decides what the
# daemon has to read before a build can start. Without it every `docker build`
# ships every node_modules in the workspace as context.
#
# It also matters for correctness, not only speed: a host `node_modules` or
# `dist` copied into the image would shadow what the build produced, so an
# image could pass while containing bytes nobody built.
#
# **Every pattern needs `**/`.** Unlike `.gitignore`, a `.dockerignore` pattern
# matches the whole path from the context root, not a basename — so a bare
# `node_modules` excludes only `/node_modules` and lets `apps/pulse/node_modules`
# and `apps/pulse/.env` straight into a layer via `COPY apps/pulse apps/pulse`.
# Found by review; the first version of this file made two guarantees it did not
# keep, one of them about secrets.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo

.git
.github

# Never let a local secrets file reach an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
